:: StoryTitle
My Wudlands Story - add a genre tag


:: StoryData
{
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.37.3",
  "start": "Start",
  "zoom": 1
}


:: StoryInit {"position":"100,100","size":"100,100"}
<!-- StoryInit sets up the story. Players never see it. -->
<!-- Before you submit: give the story a genre - on Twine's story page with all the story previews, -->
<!-- select it, then Story > Tags, such as adventure. The submit check asks for one. -->
<!-- Optional: one picture from your Images list here becomes the story's cover in the story list. -->

<!-- ********* Required ********* -->
<<set $meta_title to 'My Wudlands Story'>>
<<set $meta_description to 'One or two spoiler-free sentences for the story list.'>>
<<set $meta_author to 'Your pen name'>>
<<set $meta_maxCharNum to 1>> <!-- the largest party: 1 to 4 -->
<<set $meta_adventureTier to 1>> <!-- the level: 1 to 6 -->
<<set $meta_durationWeeks to 1>> <!-- adventure weeks it costs: 1 to 4 -->
<<set $meta_access to 'trial'>> <!-- free, trial or paid - one free story per author -->
<<set $meta_allowRunAway to true>> <!-- whether the Run away button is offered -->

<!-- Every success and failure your scenes set, each with a teaser (at most 300 characters) -->
<!-- that only the characters who reached that ending ever see. -->
<<set $meta_endings to {
  "success": "You made it through.",
  "failure": "The road was too much for you.",
  "failure:ran_away": "You turned back before the end."
}>>

<!-- ********* Your own starting values ********* -->
<<set $gold to 0>>


:: Start {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
<!-- FIRST, after the import: give the story a genre. On Twine's story page with all the -->
<!-- story previews, select this story, then Story > Tags (the button with the tag icon), -->
<!-- and add one from the genre list -->
<!-- on the tutorial page, such as adventure: the submit check asks for one, and this file -->
<!-- can't carry it. Story > Rename, next to it, gives the story its real name. -->

<!-- The first scene. Each link below leads to another scene. -->
Your story begins here.

[[Go on|Arrival]]
[[Give up|Lost]]


:: Arrival {"position":"500,25","size":"100,100"}
<!-- An ending: no links, and $isEnding says how the run ended. -->
<!-- A name may follow after a colon, like "success:met_queen" - declare it in StoryInit too. -->
You arrive safely.
<<set $isEnding to "success">>


:: Lost {"position":"500,175","size":"100,100"}
You lose your way.
<<set $isEnding to "failure">>


:: Retreat {"position":"300,325","size":"100,100"}
<!-- Only the Run away button opens this scene: no scene may link here. -->
<!-- It may lead on to more scenes; every ending of the Retreat story is a failure. -->
You turn back.
<<set $isEnding to "failure:ran_away">>


:: LastResort {"position":"500,325","size":"100,100"}
<!-- The platform sends a run here when something breaks, and the player gets the run back. -->
<!-- No links, and nothing links here. -->
The path ahead collapses. You return home empty-handed.
<<set $isEnding to "lastresort">>
